Not used from upstream (on purpose): floppy_track.sv (LGPL v3, Sorgelig; the track window is a2_trk.vhd), sdram*.v, the hdmi/ and misc/ board parts,
hdd.vhd (the hard disk card is a2_hdd.vhd, T89.1), ssc.vhd (out, T89 section 4), gen_uart.v / uart6551 (SSC), mockingboard/ (phase 2, Q7; via6522.vhd carries "do not copy without written permission"
and is never to be used), keyboard.vhd (USB scan codes; the C64 matrix table is a2_keys), gowin_* wrappers, roms/*.mi and every ROM-carrying
VHDL file (disk_ii_rom.vhd, hdd_rom.vhd, ssc_rom.vhd, applemouse_rom.vhd, applemouse_mcu_rom.vhd).
Not used from Apple-II_MiSTer (github.com/MiSTer-devel/Apple-II_MiSTer): nothing (T89 Q2: no composite decoder).

Apple-IIgs_MiSTer (https://github.com/MiSTer-devel/Apple-IIgs_MiSTer, commit 9adbba8622f378253765b7d438b6cbcc4d03fc57, 2026-07-12; GPL v3 or later, the
README lists rtl/hdd.v and rtl/roms/hdd.a65 as GPL v2 or later AppleWin code; T89.1). Taken: rtl/roms/hdd.a65 (above). Behaviours read from rtl/hdd.v
(a2_hdd.vhd) and rtl/flux_drive.v (drive_ii.vhd: the 56 clock bit cell, the quarter track head, the position that wraps at the bit count, the weak bit rule of the
MC3470, random flux on an unformatted track, bits written by read-modify-write) and re-implemented, no text copied. Not used: iwm_flux.v, iwm_woz.v,
woz_floppy_controller.sv, smartport_dev.v (an IWM chip model, WOZ parsing in gateware, 3.5" and SmartPort: T89.1 section 3 says why).
